Hall of Fame‡


# OFFICIALS #

Referee:  [LINK: (Bob McElwee) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bob_McElwee]  #95 first Super Bowl on field; alternate for XVII

Umpire:  [LINK: (Al Conway) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Al_Conway]  #27 fourth Super Bowl (IX, XIV, XVI)

Head linesman:  [LINK: (Dale Hamer) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dale_Hamer]  #104 second Super Bowl (XVII); alternate referee for XXVII

Line judge: Jack Fette #39 fifth Super Bowl (V, VIII, X, XIII)

Back judge:  [LINK: (Al Jury) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Al_Jury]  #106 second Super Bowl (XX)

Side judge:  [LINK: (Don Wedge) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Don_Wedge]  #28 first Super Bowl

Field judge:  [LINK: (Johnny Grier) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Johnny_Grier]  #23 first and only Super Bowl

Alternate referee:  [LINK: (Jerry Markbreit) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jerry_Markbreit]  #9 alternate for XIX; four Super Bowls (XVII, XXI, XXVI, XXIX) on field

Alternate umpire: Ben Montgomery #117 worked two Super Bowls on field as a line judge (XXXII & XXXVIII)

Following this game, Johnny Grier was promoted to referee, becoming the first African-American to lead an NFL officiating crew.

In addition to Grier, Dale Hamer was promoted to referee in 1989. Don Wedge was a referee from 1976 to 1978 before becoming a side judge in 1979 (he was a back judge from 1972 to 1975).

Jack Fette retired following this game and became a replay official. He was the second official, after  [LINK: (Tom Kelleher) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tom_Kelleher_(American_football)] , to officiate in five Super Bowls.


